# bits-ui

Use **bits-ui** for interactive primitives. Do not hand-roll Tabs, Pagination, Dialog, Popover, Combobox, Select, or Command.

## When

Pagination, tabs, dialogs, popovers, combobox/select, command palettes, and similar controls.

## How

Wrap bits-ui in a thin local component. Style with `cn()` plus `tabTrigger`, `controlBase`, and related tokens. Add `cursor-pointer` via `interactive` / `tabTrigger`.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { Pagination } from 'bits-ui';
	import { cn } from '$lib/cn';
	import { tabTrigger } from '$lib/variants';
</script>

<Pagination.Root {count} {perPage} {page} onPageChange={onPage}>
	{#snippet children({ pages })}
		<Pagination.Page class={cn(tabTrigger, 'size-9')} page={pageItem}>{pageItem.value}</Pagination.Page>
	{/snippet}
</Pagination.Root>
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — custom Prev/1/2/Next buttons, raw tab buttons -->
<button onclick={() => page = page + 1}>Next</button>
<button data-state={tab === 'chat' ? 'active' : undefined}>Chat</button>
```

Landing must not import app `$lib/components`. Duplicate a thin wrapper in `packages/landing/src/lib/components` when needed.
